# Skipped by Makefile.workflow's generic build: scanner.
#
# The nous binary is distributed signed + notarized via `make nous-bootstrap`
# (or `make nous-install-notarized` for the full distribution flow).
# Overwriting bin/nous with an unsigned local build at the same path
# invalidates the operator's macOS keychain ACL grants for the signed
# identity and breaks notification capabilities (UNUserNotificationCenter
# filters unsigned binaries).
#
# Build a local signed copy via `make nous-build` + `make nous-sign` when
# you need to iterate on the binary's behavior. The generic `make build`
# scanner intentionally leaves bin/nous alone.
#
# This sentinel mechanism replaces the hardcoded `case "$$name" in nous)`
# skip that used to live in Makefile.workflow's build: target. See
# workshop/issues/000032 (ariadne) for the layering rationale.
